<!--
    angr ReturnDuplicatorHigh, per-edge const narrowing extended to the WIDE
    multi-way SWITCH const-phi return (option switchreturn, default-OFF; ELEM 4112),
    S8 goto-quality sub-stage.  The direct continuation of ActionEarlyReturn.

    ActionSwitchReturn peels each CONSTANT case arm of a shared switch-dispatch
    RETURN block (v = MULTIEQUAL(#K0, #K1, ...); return v) into its own per-case
    return K, via the SAME earlyreturn_const_edges + node_split machinery
    (const_return_peel) earlyreturn uses, but with the in-edge cap lifted (256 vs
    earlyreturn's 16) so the WIDE dispatch table earlyreturn structurally skips is
    reached.  earlyreturn (default-ON) ALREADY hoists switches with <= 16
    predecessors; this witness is a 17-case dispatch (18 in-edges counting the
    default), > earlyreturn's MAX_EARLYRETURN_INEDGES=16, so earlyreturn leaves it
    merged and ONLY switchreturn changes it: the test toggles switchreturn alone,
    earlyreturn stays at its default.

    Witness (self-contained, no relocations): a 17-case dense jump-table switch,
    every case landing a constant in the return register and jumping to one exit
    epilogue, the exact shape of libedit tty__getcharindex (@0x1f145) that motivated
    the pass.  Source (gcc -O0 -no-pie, absolute-linked so the RIP-relative table
    needs no relocation):

        unsigned long f(unsigned int x) {
            switch (x) {
                case 0:  return 0;     case 9:  return 0xe;
                case 1:  return 1;     case 10: return 0xa;
                case 2:  return 2;     case 11: return 0xc;
                case 3:  return 3;     case 12: return 0xd;
                case 4:  return 4;     case 13: return 0xf;
                case 5:  return 0xb;   case 14: return 6;
                case 6:  return 0x10;  case 15: return 5;
                case 7:  return 8;     case 16: return 7;
                case 8:  return 9;     default: return 0xffffffff;
            }
        }

    At -O0 every case compiles to `mov $K, %eax; jmp .Lepilogue`, merged at one
    `pop %rbp; ret`, so kuna reconstructs `eax = MULTIEQUAL(#0, #1, ..., #-1); return
    eax` in the exit block, kept structurally by default as the merged switch below.
    Bytes [0x401106, 0x4011b8) of the linked executable; the 4-byte-relative jump
    table (17 entries) at 0x402004.

    Pass 1 (option switchreturn off, the default): kuna keeps the merged dispatch,
    `switch (a0) { case 0: v1 = 0; break; ... } return v1;`, one trailing `return v1`
    reached from every case; the default constant 0xffffffff is a plain assignment
    (`v1 = 0xffffffff`), NOT a return.
    Pass 2 (option switchreturn on): every constant case arm is peeled to its own
    return (`case 0: return 0; ... default: return 0xffffffff;`), the switch head
    preserved and the merged `return v1` gone; the `// switch-return` line is
    logged exactly once.
-->
